{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794527277531,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd82d2bffesgmtqJzwimUFtJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d22931cc002CAG8H0SM92HKvk","sessionID":"ses_e2dd82d2bffesgmtqJzwimUFtJ","messageID":"msg_1d2292265001vw41rBo03Qk5tg","type":"tool","id":"call_da6500d8b1c84eedbdee9fbd","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md","offset":40,"limit":50},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 40-89\n40: Build the Spec Kit first. The runtimes' session hooks load this build.\n41: \n42: ```bash\n43: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit install\n44: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build\n45: ```\n46: \n47: Then build the Skill Advisor. Its build uses the Spec Kit's TypeScript compiler, so it comes second. The last command checks the advisor's CLI. `list-tools` answers offline, with no daemon running.\n48: \n49: ```bash\n50: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n51: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n52: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json\n53: ```\n54: \n55: ### Check the Install\n56: \n57: Open the repository in any of the six runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin or Pi. Then run:\n58: \n59: ```\n60: /doctor:setup\n61: ```\n62: \n63: It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n64: \n65: Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n66: \n67: ### Add Code Mode\n68: \n69: Code Mode is the bridge your runtime uses to call external MCP tools. It builds separately from the two builds above. Run:\n70: \n71: ```\n72: /doctor:mcp install\n73: ```\n74: \n75: It installs the dependencies and builds Code Mode when its `dist` is missing or stale. It configures the `.utcp_config.json` manuals. It registers Code Mode in the seven project config files, two of them for Claude. Each write waits for its own approval. Add `--runtime <name>` to register one runtime only: `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `pi` or `devin`.\n76: \n77: To check Code Mode later, run `/doctor:mcp debug`. It reports PASS, WARN or FAIL per check, and `--fix` adds guided repair. Provider keys live in `.env`, which only Code Mode reads. Section 1 of [`.env.example`](.env.example) lists them. An agent cannot read that file: the [dotenv guard](.skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/README.md) refuses it on every runtime and offers key names or a fingerprint instead. The [Code Mode install guide](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/INSTALL-GUIDE.md) covers the manual steps.\n78: \n79: ### Git Hooks\n80: \n81: The first AI session installs the repository's git hooks. The root README's [Git Hooks](README.md#git-hooks) section says what each hook blocks. `/doctor:git setup` checks the hooks and the sk-git settings.\n82: \n83: Your checkout is ready once `/doctor:setup` passes. Run `/doctor:setup` again whenever something looks wrong. To use Skilled in a project of your own, pick a way in below.\n84: \n85: ---\n86: \n87: ## 3. LINK IT INTO YOUR PROJECT\n88: \n89: ### Step 1: Run the Install Guide\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 90]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 40-89\n40: Build the Spec Kit first. The runtimes' session hooks load this build.\n41: \n42: ```bash\n43: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit install\n44: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build\n45: ```\n46: \n47: Then build the Skill Advisor. Its build uses the Spec Kit's TypeScript compiler, so it comes second. The last command checks the advisor's CLI. `list-tools` answers offline, with no daemon running.\n48: \n49: ```bash\n50: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n51: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n52: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json\n53: ```\n54: \n55: ### Check the Install\n56: \n57: Open the repository in any of the six runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin or Pi. Then run:\n58: \n59: ```\n60: /doctor:setup\n61: ```\n62: \n63: It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n64: \n65: Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n66: \n67: ### Add Code Mode\n68: \n69: Code Mode is the bridge your runtime uses to call external MCP tools. It builds separately from the two builds above. Run:\n70: \n71: ```\n72: /doctor:mcp install\n73: ```\n74: \n75: It installs the dependencies and builds Code Mode when its `dist` is missing or stale. It configures the `.utcp_config.json` manuals. It registers Code Mode in the seven project config files, two of them for Claude. Each write waits for its own approval. Add `--runtime <name>` to register one runtime only: `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `pi` or `devin`.\n76: \n77: To check Code Mode later, run `/doctor:mcp debug`. It reports PASS, WARN or FAIL per check, and `--fix` adds guided repair. Provider keys live in `.env`, which only Code Mode reads. Section 1 of [`.env.example`](.env.example) lists them. An agent cannot read that file: the [dotenv guard](.skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/README.md) refuses it on every runtime and offers key names or a fingerprint instead. The [Code Mode install guide](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/INSTALL-GUIDE.md) covers the manual steps.\n78: \n79: ### Git Hooks\n80: \n81: The first AI session installs the repository's git hooks. The root README's [Git Hooks](README.md#git-hooks) section says what each hook blocks. `/doctor:git setup` checks the hooks and the sk-git settings.\n82: \n83: Your checkout is ready once `/doctor:setup` passes. Run `/doctor:setup` again whenever something looks wrong. To use Skilled in a project of your own, pick a way in below.\n84: \n85: ---\n86: \n87: ## 3. LINK IT INTO YOUR PROJECT\n88: \n89: ### Step 1: Run the Install Guide\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 90]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":50}"},"time":{"start":1794527277516,"end":1794527277531}}}}
