{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794527326019,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd82d2bffesgmtqJzwimUFtJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d229e94d002ctyRd3oMI1mwXa","sessionID":"ses_e2dd82d2bffesgmtqJzwimUFtJ","messageID":"msg_1d229d2ea001535gyn6kw2J5vP","type":"tool","id":"call_43d657f651524defa049ad59","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md","oldString":"Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n\n### Add Code Mode","newString":"Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n\nCodex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n\n### Add Code Mode"},"output":"Edited INSTALL-SKILLED.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"INSTALL-SKILLED.md","patch":"Index: INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n===================================================================\n--- INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n+++ INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n@@ -63,8 +63,10 @@\n It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n \n Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n \n+Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n+\n ### Add Code Mode\n \n Code Mode is the bridge your runtime uses to call external MCP tools. It builds separately from the two builds above. Run:\n \n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited INSTALL-SKILLED.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\",\"oldString\":\"Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\\n\\n### Add Code Mode\",\"newString\":\"Codex, Cursor and Pi spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\\n\\nCodex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\\n\\n### Add Code Mode\"}"},"time":{"start":1794527324493,"end":1794527326019}}}}
