{"type":"text","timestamp":1794527349828,"sessionID":"ses_e2dd82d2bffesgmtqJzwimUFtJ","part":{"id":"prt_1d22a43d9002LuzMCOi677dw7h","sessionID":"ses_e2dd82d2bffesgmtqJzwimUFtJ","messageID":"msg_1d22a32b1001hke5bn1qU71eii","type":"text","text":"T009 is complete. One paragraph added to `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` under `### Check the Install`, after the hyphenated-commands line.\n\n**Verify output** (run from the repo root, exit status shown per command):\n\n```\nrg -n \"codex-hooks-approved\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n67:Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\nexit=0\n\nrg -c \"trusted_hash\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n1\nexit=0\n```\n\nBoth expected values hold: one matching line and a count of 1.\n\n**Scoped diff:** `git diff --stat -- INSTALL-SKILLED.md` reports `1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)`, the paragraph plus its separating blank line. No other file touched.\n\n**Status:** the task checkbox in `tasks.md` is unticked, as instructed. The `sk-doc` compiled router returned `defer` for this prose insertion, so I followed the guide's existing voice and structure directly. Nothing is blocked on the operator.","time":{"start":1794527347673,"end":1794527349828}}}
